{"t": 1791930361.934, "event": "browser-page", "seen": [], "at": 685, "said": "Open this page from your group\u2019s link. To make your group, paste this line in a terminal on your computer: it gets svrngs and opens your home page, where you make your group and invite people to it. curl -fsSL http://localhost:57930/install.sh | sh -s -- 'http://localhost:57930/' Copy What\u2019s your name? Everyone in sees it. Join Yes Not now", "line": "curl -fsSL http://localhost:57930/install.sh | sh -s -- 'http://localhost:57930/'"}
{"t": 1791930363.43, "event": "line", "who": "sam", "exit": 0, "ms": 1496, "said": ["Getting svrngs for this computer from http://localhost:57930/get/svrngs-darwin-aarch64.tar.gz", "Checked: svrngs-darwin-aarch64.tar.gz matches SHA256SUMS.", "Installed svrngs in /tmp/start-story/sam/.local/bin.", "/tmp/start-story/sam/.local/bin is not on your PATH, so to run svrngs yourself type /tmp/start-story/sam/.local/bin/svrngs; nothing else needs it.", "svrngs runs now, and whenever you log in (/tmp/start-story/sam/Library/LaunchAgents/sh.svrnme.svrngs.plist).", "Your home page, the same address each time svrngs starts: http://svrngs.localhost:57984/"], "open_asked": "http://svrngs.localhost:57984/", "open_ms": 1489}
{"t": 1791930395.5, "event": "browser-make", "seen": [], "before": {"at": 2526, "said": "Your groups This page is yours, on this computer alone. On it you see your groups and who is in each, open what the people in them lend you, each in a tab of its own beside this page, open each group\u2019s folder, make a group, make a link to invite someone or to add your phone or another computer, and choose how many people at once may use what this computer lends them. A link works for a day, while this computer is on. Making one stops the last link you made letting anyone new in; everyone it let in stays. A program on this computer, such as one you chat with a friend\u2019s model in, reaches what"}, "pressed": 2596, "made": null, "after": {"at": 32873, "said": "Your groups This page is yours, on this computer alone. On it you see your groups and who is in each, open what the people in them lend you, each in a tab of its own beside this page, open each group\u2019s folder, make a group, make a link to invite someone or to add your phone or another computer, and choose how many people at once may use what this computer lends them. A link works for a day, while this computer is on. Making one stops the last link you made letting anyone new in; everyone it let in stays. A program on this computer, such as one you chat with a friend\u2019s model in, reaches what", "folder": "Lab\u2019s folder is on this computer at /Users/alexsbryan/svrngs/Lab"}, "linked": 32929, "link_at": 33219, "link": "http://localhost:57930/#<the token>", "link_said": "Send this link to the person you are inviting: http://localhost:57930/#<the token> It opens in a browser, which says how to join from there. It works for a day, while this computer is on. Copy the link"}
{"t": 1791930395.509, "event": "command", "who": "sam", "typed": "~/.local/bin/svrngs share 18089", "exit": 1, "said": "svrngs: say what is on port 18089: `svrngs share 18089 --kind <kind>`, its own name if it is one svrngs knows: jellyfin, navidrome, calibre-web, llama-server", "ms": 7}
{"t": 1791930395.516, "event": "command", "who": "sam", "typed": "~/.local/bin/svrngs share 18089 --kind llama-server", "exit": 0, "said": "Lent llama-server (port 18089) to everyone in your groups, as many at once as want it. To let fewer in at once, change it on your home page, or `svrngs share 18089 --limit <number>`.\nThey cannot open /slots, /v1/stream, /v1/streams, /v1/chat/completions/control, /lora-adapters, /metrics, /tools, /cors-proxy, /models: svrngs keeps these back whenever a llama-server is lent, since they show one person's use of it to the others or change it for everyone.\nsvrngs is running here already, so they can open it now.\n`svrngs unshare llama-server` stops lending it.\nIf llama-server takes a password on each request, paste what it takes in its Authorization header, then press Enter (Enter alone for none):", "ms": 7}
